{
  "_comment": "The result set (owner, 2026-10-15 and 2026-10-20): after linking, the per-file lift and scratch routing, core computes what a plan will leave, and every preview ends with it. A step's files: its explicit output (one per input file it runs over, or one for a join; a name only when it runs over one file and the output is no pattern), else what its tool's `produces:` names (an {arg} value is an extension, a {format} a fixed one, a kind is shown as a kind), else each input's own extension. Outputs in the run scratch (`scratch`) and steps of readonly or control tools leave nothing. Up to 3 files, all named: by name; otherwise counts by type in first-seen order. A named file whose extension disagrees with its tool's declaration is flagged. Nothing left: an empty line (no preview line). `same_for` is the batch preview's line after the first file's steps (owner: first file in full, then the rest). Python `knaif.result_set`, Rust `knaif_core::result_set`.",
  "tables": {
    "ffmpeg": {
      "file_kinds": {"mp4": "video", "mov": "video", "mkv": "video", "gif": "video", "mp3": "audio", "wav": "audio", "jpg": "image", "png": "image"},
      "produces": {"convert_video": {"arg": "container"}, "compress_video": {"format": "mp4"}, "extract_audio": "audio", "create_thumbnail": "image"},
      "readonly": [],
      "joining": ["concat_video"]
    },
    "documents": {
      "file_kinds": {"pdf": "document", "docx": "document", "txt": "text"},
      "produces": {"extract_text": "text", "convert_document": {"arg": "to_format"}},
      "readonly": ["inspect_document", "extract_text", "find_in_document"],
      "joining": ["merge_pdfs"]
    }
  },
